  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Nutrition security Scoping and Ideation Assignment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The scoping and ideation assignment is a short term consultancy task that aims to inform new programming for food and nutrition security activities under the new MACS 2026-2029. This assignment aims to carryout an analysis of the horticulture, livestock and fisheries value chains, applying the food systems framework, also integrating a water-energy-food nexus approach. For this the analysis will comprise  a comprehensive review of the Kenyan agrifood policy context, pinpointing policy and development priorities in relation to the shared interests with the Netherlands government&apos;s interest as outlined in the current foreign policy. The assignment will also analyse the development partners&apos; landscape in the agrifood sector highlighting the key actors and trends, also inview of the Dutch diamond partner approach. The comprehensive analysis will lead to the development of highlevel Theory of change for new programming, an EOI and scoring template as well as potential implementing partners.</narrative>
  </description>
